hw/sh4: ze0 2DG op 0x44 adds to the local offset (TODO M8.C1g).

Once the AuiApp shell runs (M8.C1g) its lists use op 0x44 XY, which
ze0-0014 skipped as unknown: 44000000 000001e0 moves the local offset
down by one 480-line page and 44000000 0000fe20 moves it back, so the
two-page AUI surface (800x2400) is drawn page by page.  The op adds XY
to the offset set by 0x40.  With gfx-trace=on every write of the
target-surface register (+0x50) is logged as `ze0-2dg: target ADDR`.

Signed-off-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>


diff --git a/hw/sh4/ze0_2dg.c b/hw/sh4/ze0_2dg.c
index dc305bf0d..44a0517c0 100644
--- a/hw/sh4/ze0_2dg.c
+++ b/hw/sh4/ze0_2dg.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
  *   0x30xxxxxx OFF        call: push return, pc = op address + OFF
  *   0x38xxxxxx 0          return
  *   0x40xxxxxx XY         local coordinate offset
+ *   0x44xxxxxx XY         add XY to the local offset (AuiApp page flips)
  *   0x18000600 N<<16|R OFF  write N+1 registers from R, data at op + OFF
  *   0x18xxxxxx N<<16|R V0..VN  write N+1 registers from R
  *   0x28xxxxxx LEN        skip LEN bytes (inline data)
@@ -69,6 +70,9 @@ static void reg_set(Dl *d, uint32_t off, uint32_t v)
     if (off < ZE0_GFX_SIZE - 4) {
         stl_le_p((uint8_t *)d->r + off, v);
     }
+    if (off == 0x50 && d->s->trace) {
+        qemu_log_mask(LOG_UNIMP, "ze0-2dg: target 0x%08x\n", v);
+    }
 }
 
